The CRI-O logs identify the root cause.

Root cause

The fatal error is:

Failed to start streaming server:
listen tcp [2405:100:200:72:881e:df7b:f42e:9621]:0:
bind: cannot assign requested address

CRI-O is trying to bind its streaming server to the IPv6 address:

2405:100:200:72:881e:df7b:f42e:9621

but that IPv6 address is not currently configured on any interface after the reboot. Because CRI-O cannot bind to it, it exits, and since kubelet depends on CRI-O, kubelet never starts.


---

First, verify whether the IPv6 address exists

Run:

ip -6 addr

and

ip addr

Check whether you can find:

2405:100:200:72:881e:df7b:f42e:9621

If it is missing, that's exactly why CRI-O fails.


---

Find where this address is configured

Run:

grep -R "2405:100:200:72:881e:df7b:f42e:9621" /etc/crio /etc/systemd /etc/kubernetes /etc

and

grep -R "stream-address" /etc/crio

The log shows:

FLAG: --stream-address="2405:100:200:72:881e:df7b:f42e:9621"

We need to determine which MachineConfig or CRI-O configuration set this value.


---

Also inspect the CRI-O drop-ins

Since you have:

/etc/systemd/system/crio.service.d/
  01-kubens.conf
  05-mco-ordering.conf
  10-mco-default-madv.conf
  10-mco-profile-unix-socket.conf
  20-nodenet.conf

show the contents of:

cat /etc/systemd/system/crio.service.d/20-nodenet.conf

and

cat /etc/systemd/system/crio.service.d/10-mco-profile-unix-socket.conf

Also check:

grep -R stream_address /etc/crio

or

grep -R stream-address /etc/crio


---

My suspicion

Earlier, your cluster had PerformanceProfile, Node Tuning Operator, and SR-IOV MachineConfigs. After the MCP reconciled, a new rendered MachineConfig was created. One of those MachineConfigs may have changed the CRI-O stream-address to a specific IPv6 address that is no longer present after reboot.

Please share the outputs of:

ip -6 addr
cat /etc/systemd/system/crio.service.d/20-nodenet.conf
grep -R "stream-address" /etc/crio

Those three outputs should pinpoint exactly why CRI-O is binding to an unavailable IPv6 address.
